  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DIAKONIA, Bridge 2022-2023 - New DIAKONIA DDHH and Gender</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">DIAKONIA, Bridge 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Syftet med denna insats &#xE4;r att st&#xE4;rka och st&#xF6;dja det civila samh&#xE4;llet, s&#xE4;rskilt kvinnorganisationer, och HBTQ-grupper i Bolivia. Insatserna kommer att inriktas p&#xE5; att st&#xE4;rka gruppernas r&#xE4;ttigheter, s&#xE4;rskilt m&#xF6;jligheter till politiskt deltagande och inflytande, sexuella och reproduktiva r&#xE4;ttigheter och kampen mot k&#xF6;nsrelaterat v&#xE5;ld, inklusive m&#xE4;nniskohandel. For perioden 2022-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this effort is focus on strengthening and support civil society organizations, especially women&#xB4;s organizations and HBTQ groups in Bolivia. during the period 2022-2023</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The General objective of Diakonias strategy: Contribute to the development of a strong and empowered civil society (SC), where diverse organizations and marginalized populations actively participate in local, departmental and/or national development and promote social and gender justice to eradicate inequalities.

The specific objective of this support is:

Secure the achieved results, end processes from the previous development and connect it to future processes by focusing on strengthening the partners, reviewing processes and resources and coordinating dialogue between civil society actors.</narrative>
  </description>
